course: dictionary
lesson: 7238
title: Short words, short names
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Informal words are shortened words people use in speech, texts and on social media. Pic is short for picture, so a pic is a photo or image. «Send me a pic!» means send me a photo.
explain: Watch out: pic is not always a word on its own. In «Long words are read in chunks called syllables, the beats you can clap: sand-wich, pic-nic, fan-tas-tic», the first part of pic-nic is just one chunk of a longer word. Context helps you tell them apart.
explain: Read the clues around the word. If someone writes «Nice pic!» under your post, they mean a nice photo. In the UK and Australia, «Let's go to the pics tonight» means going to watch a film, because pics is short for pictures, an informal name for films.
fact: Pic is informal, so use it in chatty messages, not in formal writing.
fact: «Pic» means a photo or picture, short for picture.
fact: A «profile pic» is the photo that shows who you are on an online account.
fact: In the UK and Australia, «the pics» is an informal word for the cinema or films.
fact: In «pic-nic», the pic is just a chunk of the word, the first beat of picnic.
exercise: Your friend says, «Send me a pic of the cake.» What does pic mean? | *A photo of the cake | A slice of cake, cut into pieces | A cake recipe | A photo
exercise: In the word «pic-nic», what is pic? | A film about a park | *Just a chunk of the word, not a photo | A photo of the food
exercise: Ali says, «Let's go to the pics tonight.» In the UK, what might Ali mean? | *Going to the cinema to watch a film | Going to draw pictures at home | Going to take photos in the park | Going to buy a new phone
test: What is a «profile pic»? | A video you send to a friend | A map of your street | A painting of your house | *The photo that shows who you are on an online account
test: Which phrase means take a photo? | Take a nap | Take a bow | Take a seat | *Take a pic
exam: Mia writes «Nice pic!» under your post. What does she mean? | *She likes your photo | She is going to the cinema with you | She wants to borrow your bike | She thinks your homework is late
